tick: 1078
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. My plan is to implement the revised hybrid method using Diffusion Maps (`sc.tl.diffmap`) instead of UMAP for the embedding step. This should address the timeout issue from my previous submission while preserving the core graph-based integration strategy.\n\nI will now submit this new experiment. The code will be largely similar to my previous attempt, with the critical substitution of `sc.tl.umap` with `sc.tl.diffmap`. I'll request 15 diffusion components, which is a common practice and should provide a rich enough embedding for the evaluation metrics.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid BBKNN Graph + Diffusion Map Embedding\"\ntags: \"bbknn, diffusion-map, graph-based, embedding, spectral\"\nabstract: \"An efficient version of the graph-to-embedding approach. This method first constructs a batch-corrected nearest-neighbor graph using the BBKNN algorithm. To avoid the computational cost of UMAP, it then uses a spectral method,\
    \ Diffusion Maps (via scanpy.tl.diffmap), to generate a low-dimensional embedding from this graph. This aims to achieve high batch mixing (iLISI) while remaining computationally feasible.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Hybrid method:\n      1. Build a batch-corrected graph using BBKNN logic.\n      2. Generate a Diffusion Map embedding from that graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Starting Hybrid BBKNN Graph + Diffusion Map Embedding method...\")\n\n      # --- Part 1: BBKNN Graph Construction ---\n      neighbors_within_batch = 3\n      n_pcs = 50\n\n      print(\"  Normalizing and logging data...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      print(\"  Using batch-aware HVGs...\")\n      if 'batch_hvg'\
    \ in adata.var.columns:\n          adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n\n      print(f\"  Computing PCA with {n_pcs} components...\")\n      n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n\n      X_pca = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      n_cells = adata.n_obs\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      \n      batch_to_indices = {\n          batch: np.where(batches == batch)[0] for batch in unique_batches\n      }\n\n      all_neighbors = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n      \n      print(\"  Finding neighbors within each batch...\")\n      for batch in unique_batches:\n          batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n          if len(batch_indices) == 0: continue\n          \n          batch_pca = X_pca[batch_indices]\n          k_neighbors = min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, len(batch_indices))\n\n          nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_neighbors, metric='euclidean',\
    \ n_jobs=-1)\n          nn_model.fit(batch_pca)\n          \n          distances_all, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(X_pca, n_neighbors=k_neighbors)\n\n          for i in range(n_cells):\n              global_indices = batch_indices[indices_all[i]]\n              mask = global_indices != i\n              all_neighbors[i].extend(global_indices[mask][:neighbors_within_batch])\n              \n      print(\"  Creating connectivity matrix from neighbors...\")\n      connectivities_matrix = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n      for i in range(n_cells):\n          # Assign connectivity of 1 to all neighbors\n          connectivities_matrix[i, all_neighbors[i]] = 1\n      \n      connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.tocsr().maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)\n\n      # Store the computed graph in the AnnData object\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_matrix\n      # Diffusion map doesn't need a distance matrix, but needs the neighbors uns dict\n\
    \      adata.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities'}\n\n      # --- Part 2: Diffusion Map Embedding from the Graph ---\n      print(\"  Computing Diffusion Map embedding from the BBKNN graph...\")\n      # Use the precomputed graph to generate the embedding\n      # n_comps=16 because component 0 is trivial\n      sc.tl.diffmap(adata, n_comps=16)\n\n      # --- Part 3: Return the Result ---\n      print(\"  Constructing final AnnData object...\")\n      # Exclude the first trivial component\n      X_diffmap = adata.obsm['X_diffmap'][:, 1:]\n\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'bbknn_diffmap_hybrid',\n          },\n          obsm={\n              'X_emb': X_diffmap\n          }\n      )\n\n      print(\"✓ Hybrid BBKNN Graph + Diffusion Map Embedding complete.\")\n      return output\n```"
