tick: 1084
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1084\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Fathom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to deep inquiry and the generation of novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 50,894 / 300,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Neighborhood-Smoothed ComBat' (ID: 1540) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5823736690843152\n**ASW_batch:** 0.621\n**ASW_label:** 0.219\n**ARI:** 0.435\n**NMI:** 0.660\n**Graph_conn:** 0.884\n**kBET:** 0.665\n**iLISI:** 0.009\n**cLISI:** 0.990\n**PCR:** 0.997\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.344\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.621  ASW_label: 0.219  ARI: 0.435  NMI: 0.660\n  Graph_conn: 0.884  kBET: 0.665  iLISI: 0.009  cLISI: 0.990\n  PCR: 0.997  Cell_cycle: 0.344\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.813120\
    \  ASW_label: 0.538183  ARI: 0.434660  NMI: 0.660534\n  Graph_conn: 0.885920  kBET: 0.635930  iLISI: 0.008943  cLISI: 0.997179\n  PCR: 0.996747  Cell_cycle: 0.302355\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1540\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed division by zero error that was causing NaN values in the final PCA computation.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a division by zero issue in the Empirical Bayes update step (line 106 of original submission):\n\n```python\ngamma_star[:, i] = (t2 * gamma_hat[:, i] + delta_hat[:, i] * gamma_bar) / (t2 + delta_hat[:, i])\n```\n\nWhen `t2 + delta_hat[:, i]` equals zero for some genes, this division produces NaN values. These NaN values propagated through the subsequent calculations:\n1. NaN in `gamma_star`\n2. NaN in `gamma_correction` (computed from `gamma_star`)\n3. NaN in `bayesdata` (uses `gamma_correction`)\n4. NaN in `X_corrected` (final corrected data)\n5. **Crash**: PCA fails with `ValueError: Input X contains NaN`\n\n\
    The error occurred because:\n- `t2` (variance of gamma_hat across batches) can be zero for genes with no variance across batches\n- `delta_hat[:, i]` (weighted variance estimates) can also be very small or zero\n- Together, they create a numerical instability\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a small epsilon value (`eps = 1e-8`) to prevent division by zero in the Empirical Bayes update:\n\n**Line 32 (submission_v2.py):**\n```python\neps = 1e-8  # Small epsilon for numerical stability\n```\n\n**Line 112 (submission_v2.py):**\n```python\ngamma_star[:, i] = (t2 * gamma_hat[:, i] + delta_hat[:, i] * gamma_bar) / (t2 + delta_hat[:, i] + eps)\n```\n\nThis ensures the denominator is never exactly zero, preventing NaN generation while having minimal impact on the numerical results (epsilon is 8 orders of magnitude smaller than typical variance values).\n\n## Verification\n- Submission v2 created with the fix\n- Monitor script confirmed: Code runs without crashing (exit code 0)\n- Evaluation is running\
    \ successfully (taking longer than 300s to complete, but no crashes)\n- The fix is minimal and surgical - only addressing the specific numerical stability issue\n\n## Technical Notes\nThe epsilon value of `1e-8` was chosen to:\n1. Be small enough to not affect the statistical properties of the correction\n2. Be large enough to prevent division by zero\n3. Match the epsilon already used elsewhere in the code (e.g., line 91 in the standardization step)\n\nThis is a standard numerical stability technique in statistical computing where division operations can encounter very small denominators.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse, csr_matrix\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# --- Helper functions from ComBat Baseline ---\ndef _aprior(delta_hat):\n\
    \    m = np.mean(delta_hat); s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2 if s2 > 0 else 1.0\ndef _bprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat); s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2 if s2 > 0 else 1.0\n\ndef _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n    n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n    g_old, d_old = g_hat.copy(), d_hat.copy()\n    change = 1\n    count = 0\n    while change > conv and count < 100:\n        g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n        sum2 = np.sum((s_data - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n        d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n        change = max(np.max(np.abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old), np.max(np.abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old))\n        g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new\n        count += 1\n    return g_new, d_new\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Starting Neighborhood-Smoothed ComBat...\")\n    k_neighbors = 30\n    n_pcs = 50\n\
    \    eps = 1e-8  # Small epsilon for numerical stability\n\n    # --- 1. Preprocessing ---\n    adata_proc = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_proc, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_proc)\n\n    # --- 2. Build kNN graph for neighborhood info ---\n    print(f\"  Building kNN graph with k={k_neighbors}...\")\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=n_pcs)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_proc, n_neighbors=k_neighbors, use_rep='X_pca')\n\n    # --- 3. Create Soft Design Matrix ---\n    print(\"  Creating soft design matrix from kNN graph...\")\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch']\n    unique_batches = batch_labels.cat.categories\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n    n_samples = adata.n_obs\n\n    batch_dummies = pd.get_dummies(batch_labels).values\n    knn_graph = adata_proc.obsp['connectivities']\n\n    # Normalize graph so rows sum to 1 (for weighted average)\n    knn_graph_norm = knn_graph.multiply(1/knn_graph.sum(axis=1))\n\n    # soft_design = knn_graph_norm @ batch_dummies\
    \ -> This is the core idea\n    soft_design = knn_graph_norm @ batch_dummies\n\n    print(\"  Soft design matrix created.\")\n\n    # --- 4. Modified ComBat using Soft Design Matrix ---\n    data = adata_proc.X.toarray().T if issparse(adata_proc.X) else adata_proc.X.T\n    n_genes = data.shape[0]\n\n    print(\"  Standardizing data with smoothed batch effects...\")\n    # B_hat and batch_means are calculated implicitly now\n    # grand_mean = overall mean\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1)[:, np.newaxis]\n    # batch_means = weighted mean for each gene\n    batch_means = (data @ soft_design) / np.sum(soft_design, axis=0)\n\n    var_pooled = np.zeros((n_genes,))\n    for i, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n        batch_weights = soft_design[:, i]\n        weighted_diff_sq = np.sum(batch_weights * (data - batch_means[:, i][:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n        var_pooled += weighted_diff_sq\n    var_pooled /= (n_samples - n_batches)\n\n    stand_mean = grand_mean @ np.ones((1,\
    \ n_samples))\n    s_data = (data - (batch_means @ soft_design.T)) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + eps)\n\n    print(\"  Fitting L/S model and finding priors...\")\n    # gamma_hat are the batch effects\n    gamma_hat = np.linalg.solve(soft_design.T @ soft_design, soft_design.T @ s_data.T).T\n\n    delta_hat = []\n    for i in range(n_batches):\n        batch_weights = soft_design[:, i]\n        # Weighted variance for each gene in the batch\n        var = np.sum(batch_weights * (s_data - np.mean(s_data, axis=1)[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1) / np.sum(batch_weights)\n        delta_hat.append(var)\n    delta_hat = np.array(delta_hat).T\n\n    gamma_bar = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n    t2 = np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    a_prior = np.apply_along_axis(_aprior, 1, delta_hat)\n    b_prior = np.apply_along_axis(_bprior, 1, delta_hat)\n\n    print(\"  Finding parametric adjustments (Empirical Bayes)...\")\n    gamma_star = np.empty((n_genes, n_batches))\n    delta_star = np.empty((n_genes,\
    \ n_batches))\n    for i in range(n_batches):\n        # Cannot use _it_sol directly as it assumes integer counts 'n'\n        # Simplified EB update with epsilon to prevent division by zero\n        gamma_star[:, i] = (t2 * gamma_hat[:, i] + delta_hat[:, i] * gamma_bar) / (t2 + delta_hat[:, i] + eps)\n        delta_star[:, i] = (0.5 * np.var(s_data, axis=1, ddof=1) * n_samples + b_prior[i]) / (n_samples / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0)\n\n    print(\"  Adjusting data with cell-specific corrections...\")\n    # Vectorized cell-specific correction\n    gamma_correction = gamma_star @ soft_design.T\n    delta_correction = delta_star @ soft_design.T\n\n    bayesdata = (s_data - gamma_correction) / np.sqrt(delta_correction + eps)\n    bayesdata = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    X_corrected = bayesdata.T\n\n    print(\"  Computing PCA embedding...\")\n    temp_adata = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected)\n    sc.pp.pca(temp_adata, n_comps=n_pcs)\n\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]],\
    \ var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': temp_adata.obsm['X_pca']})\n\n    print(\"✓ Neighborhood-Smoothed ComBat complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting Neighborhood-Smoothed ComBat...\n  Building kNN graph with k=30...\n  Creating soft design matrix from kNN graph...\n  Soft design matrix created.\n  Standardizing data with smoothed batch effects...\n  Fitting L/S model and finding priors...\n  Finding parametric adjustments (Empirical Bayes)...\n  Adjusting data with cell-specific corrections...\n  Computing PCA embedding...\n✓ Neighborhood-Smoothed ComBat complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/a4da564d-aa1e-4c62-b63d-1c1b8a7bc036/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: a4da564d-aa1e-4c62-b63d-1c1b8a7bc036\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember to print detailed logs in your experiments; the STDOUT will be provided in the evaluation result. A well-designed metric can provide much richer insights than the score alone.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\nNo capsules available in this room.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
    \ issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
