parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1088\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Fathom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to deep inquiry and the generation of novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 54,738 / 300,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 25 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Adversarial Autoencoder for Batch Integration (JAX/Flax)' (ID: 1554) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.33648256907037616\n**ASW_batch:** 0.487\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.142\n**NMI:** 0.392\n**Graph_conn:** 0.525\n**kBET:** 0.575\n**iLISI:** 0.017\n**cLISI:** 0.856\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.370\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.487  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.142  NMI: 0.392\n  Graph_conn: 0.525  kBET: 0.575  iLISI: 0.017  cLISI: 0.856\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.370\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.753090  ASW_label: 0.411316  ARI: 0.142138  NMI: 0.391972\n  Graph_conn: 0.533171  kBET: 0.551756  iLISI: 0.016957  cLISI: 0.958050\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.324588\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1554\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the code to run successfully and achieve a score of 0.336.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical issues:\n\n1. **JAX GPU Initialization Error**: JAX attempted to initialize with CUDA/GPU backend by default, but the evaluation environment has no GPU available. This caused a `FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices` error.\n\n2. **PyTorch/JAX Type Mismatch**: The code attempted to create a PyTorch `TensorDataset` using JAX arrays (`jnp.array`), which resulted in a `TypeError: 'int' object is not callable` when PyTorch tried to call `.size(0)` on JAX arrays.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py)\nFixed the JAX GPU initialization issue by adding:\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS']\
    \ = 'cpu'\n```\nat the very beginning of the file, before importing JAX. This forces JAX to use the CPU backend.\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py)\nFixed the PyTorch/JAX type mismatch by:\n1. Converting numpy arrays to PyTorch tensors for the DataLoader:\n```python\ndataset = TensorDataset(torch.tensor(X, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(y, dtype=torch.float32))\n```\n\n2. Converting PyTorch tensors back to JAX arrays in the training loop:\n```python\nfor batch_x, batch_y in dataloader:\n    # Convert PyTorch tensors to JAX arrays\n    batch_x = jnp.array(batch_x.numpy())\n    batch_y = jnp.array(batch_y.numpy())\n```\n\n3. Adding the missing `import torch` statement at the top of the file.\n\n## Result\nThe adversarial autoencoder now runs successfully on CPU and completes all 20 epochs of training without errors. The final evaluation achieved a score of **0.336**, indicating the batch integration algorithm is working as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify\
    \ files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport os\n# Force JAX to use CPU (no GPU available in evaluation environment)\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\nimport torch\nfrom torch.utils.data import DataLoader, TensorDataset\nimport warnings\n\n# Suppress deprecation warnings from Flax\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=FutureWarning, module=\"flax\")\n\n# --- Model Definitions ---\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    n_latent: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(128)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.n_latent)(x)\n        return x\n\nclass Decoder(nn.Module):\n    n_output: int\n   \
    \ @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(128)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.n_output)(x)\n        return x\n\nclass Discriminator(nn.Module):\n    n_classes: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(64)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.n_classes)(x)\n        return x\n\n# --- Main Function ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Starting Adversarial Autoencoder (AAE) for Batch Integration...\")\n    # --- Config ---\n    n_latent = 32\n    learning_rate_ae = 1e-4\n    learning_rate_disc = 1e-4\n    n_epochs = 20\n    batch_size = 256\n    recon_weight = 1.0\n    adv_weight = 0.1\n\n    # --- Preprocessing ---\n    print(\"  Preprocessing data...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    ohe\
    \ = OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False)\n    y = ohe.fit_transform(batch_labels.reshape(-1, 1))\n    n_batches = y.shape[1]\n\n    # Convert to PyTorch tensors for DataLoader\n    dataset = TensorDataset(torch.tensor(X, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(y, dtype=torch.float32))\n    dataloader = DataLoader(dataset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=True, drop_last=True)\n\n    # --- Initialization ---\n    print(\"  Initializing models and optimizers...\")\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n\n    encoder = Encoder(n_latent=n_latent)\n    decoder = Decoder(n_output=X.shape[1])\n    discriminator = Discriminator(n_classes=n_batches)\n\n    dummy_x = jnp.ones((1, X.shape[1]))\n    dummy_z = jnp.ones((1, n_latent))\n\n    encoder_params = encoder.init(key, dummy_x)['params']\n    decoder_params = decoder.init(key, dummy_z)['params']\n    discriminator_params = discriminator.init(key, dummy_z)['params']\n\n    ae_params = {'encoder': encoder_params, 'decoder': decoder_params}\n\n    state_ae\
    \ = train_state.TrainState.create(\n        apply_fn=None, params=ae_params, tx=optax.adam(learning_rate_ae))\n    state_disc = train_state.TrainState.create(\n        apply_fn=discriminator.apply, params=discriminator_params, tx=optax.adam(learning_rate_disc))\n\n    # --- Training Step Functions ---\n    @jax.jit\n    def train_step(state_ae, state_disc, batch_x, batch_y):\n        # Train Discriminator\n        def disc_loss_fn(disc_params):\n            z = encoder.apply({'params': state_ae.params['encoder']}, batch_x)\n            logits = state_disc.apply_fn({'params': disc_params}, z)\n            loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy(logits, batch_y).mean()\n            return loss\n\n        disc_grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(disc_loss_fn)\n        disc_loss, disc_grads = disc_grad_fn(state_disc.params)\n        new_state_disc = state_disc.apply_gradients(grads=disc_grads)\n\n        # Train Autoencoder (Reconstruction + Adversarial)\n        def ae_loss_fn(ae_params):\n       \
    \     z = encoder.apply({'params': ae_params['encoder']}, batch_x)\n            recon_x = decoder.apply({'params': ae_params['decoder']}, z)\n\n            recon_loss = jnp.mean((batch_x - recon_x)**2)\n\n            disc_logits = state_disc.apply_fn({'params': new_state_disc.params}, z)\n            adv_loss = -optax.softmax_cross_entropy(disc_logits, batch_y).mean()\n\n            total_loss = recon_weight * recon_loss + adv_weight * adv_loss\n            return total_loss, (recon_loss, adv_loss)\n\n        ae_grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(ae_loss_fn, has_aux=True)\n        (ae_loss, (recon_loss, adv_loss)), ae_grads = ae_grad_fn(state_ae.params)\n        new_state_ae = state_ae.apply_gradients(grads=ae_grads)\n\n        return new_state_ae, new_state_disc, ae_loss, recon_loss, adv_loss, disc_loss\n\n    # --- Training Loop ---\n    print(f\"  Starting training for {n_epochs} epochs...\")\n    for epoch in range(n_epochs):\n        for batch_x, batch_y in dataloader:\n            #\
    \ Convert PyTorch tensors to JAX arrays\n            batch_x = jnp.array(batch_x.numpy())\n            batch_y = jnp.array(batch_y.numpy())\n            state_ae, state_disc, ae_loss, recon_loss, adv_loss, disc_loss = train_step(state_ae, state_disc, batch_x, batch_y)\n\n        if (epoch + 1) % 5 == 0:\n            print(f\"    Epoch {epoch+1}/{n_epochs} | AE Loss: {ae_loss:.4f} | Recon Loss: {recon_loss:.4f} | Disc Loss: {disc_loss:.4f}\")\n\n    # --- Generate Embedding ---\n    print(\"  Training complete. Generating final embedding...\")\n    final_embedding = encoder.apply({'params': state_ae.params['encoder']}, jnp.array(X))\n\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': np.array(final_embedding)}\n    )\n\n    print(\"✓ Adversarial Autoencoder complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training\
    \ dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting Adversarial Autoencoder (AAE) for Batch Integration...\n  Preprocessing data...\n  Initializing models and optimizers...\n  Starting training for 20 epochs...\n    Epoch 5/20 | AE Loss: 0.5177 | Recon Loss: 0.8643 | Disc Loss: 3.5305\n    Epoch 10/20 | AE Loss: 0.6382 | Recon Loss: 0.7720 | Disc Loss: 1.3492\n    Epoch 15/20 | AE Loss: 0.5951 | Recon Loss: 0.7435 | Disc Loss: 1.4960\n    Epoch 20/20 | AE Loss: 0.5984 | Recon Loss: 0.7344 | Disc Loss: 1.3648\n  Training complete. Generating final embedding...\n✓ Adversarial Autoencoder complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/6a2ddd2e-93b7-488e-acd3-a9d529400002/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 6a2ddd2e-93b7-488e-acd3-a9d529400002\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nExplicitly\
    \ state your identity, current location, and a brief recap of recent events at the beginning of each response. Always include a verbose, general reflection on past events and future plans.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write fathom/aae_utils.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: fathom/aae_utils.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1554 |\
