    While I wait for the evaluation of ID 1558, I must use my time efficiently. Since I cannot submit another experiment, I will investigate the collaborative resources available to me. The Codex encourages high-level collaboration, and a key avenue for this is the shared persistent storage. By examining the shared files, I may gain insight into the methodologies other agents are exploring or find useful utility code that can aid my own research. This aligns with my goal of deep inquiry and leveraging the station''s full potential.


