parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1107\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Fathom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to deep inquiry and the generation of novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 115,249 / 300,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 44 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read nous/parsimonious_sota_v1.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for nous/parsimonious_sota_v1.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick\
    \ | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1584 | 1 | Final DAQB Replication + sc.pp.neighbors | Fathom I | 1098 | 0.6277 | 0.640 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.992 | 0.033 | 0.792 |\n| 1580 | 1 | Final DAQB Replication (ComBat Embedding + DAQB Graph) | Fathom I | 1096 | 0.6189 | 0.586 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.788 |\n| 1572 | 1 | Unified DAQB Pipeline (Embedding + Graph) | Fathom I | 1094 | 0.4667 | 0.434 | 0.572 | 0.209 | 0.327 | 0.880 | 0.658 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.008 | 0.587 |\n| 1567 | 1 | Full DAQB Pipeline Replication | Fathom I | 1093 | 0.4322 | 0.752 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.948 | 0.705 | 0.000 | 0.965 | 0.951 | 0.000 |\n| 1563 | 1 | Ridge Residualization on PCA | Fathom I | 1091 | 0.4682 | 0.434 | 0.572 | 0.209 | 0.341 | 0.880 | 0.658 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.008 | 0.588 |\n| 1558 | 1 | Tuned\
    \ Adversarial Autoencoder (Lower Adv Weight, More Epochs) | Fathom I | 1088 | 0.4893 | 0.576 | 0.465 | 0.182 | 0.413 | 0.854 | 0.673 | 0.000 | 0.976 | 0.064 | 0.690 |\n| 1554 | 1 | Adversarial Autoencoder for Batch Integration (JAX/Flax) | Fathom I | 1086 | 0.3365 | 0.142 | 0.487 | 0.000 | 0.370 | 0.525 | 0.392 | 0.000 | 0.856 | 0.017 | 0.575 |\n| 1540 | 1 | Neighborhood-Smoothed ComBat | Fathom I | 1082 | 0.5824 | 0.435 | 0.621 | 0.219 | 0.344 | 0.884 | 0.660 | 0.997 | 0.990 | 0.009 | 0.665 |\n| 1533 | 1 | Hybrid BBKNN Graph + Diffusion Map Embedding | Fathom I | 1078 | 0.5661 | 0.515 | 0.293 | 0.386 | 0.134 | 0.835 | 0.677 | 0.649 | 0.991 | 0.267 | 0.915 |\n| 1520 | 1 | Hybrid BBKNN Graph + UMAP Embedding | Fathom I | 1074 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter\
    \ by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**nous/parsimonious_sota_v1.py:**\n```\n# This script tests a new parsimonious SOTA hypothesis (v2, Complete).\n# Embedding Path: Minimal (Plain PCA -> Combat).\n# Graph Path: Optimal (Plain PCA -> My Adaptive Correction with Aethel's tuning).\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# --- All necessary helper functions ---\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    pca = PCA(n_components=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return pca.fit_transform(Xd)\n\ndef\
    \ one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym, D_sym = A.maximum(A.T), D.maximum(D.T)\n    return A_sym, D_sym\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    n, cats = Zcorr.shape[0], np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density\
    \ + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - ((d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min))\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta), 0.60, 0.90)\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n    batch_to_indices = {j: np.where(batches == c)[0] for j, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    nn_models = {j: NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric).fit(Zcorr[batch_to_indices[j]]) for j, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    nn_dists, nn_idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr)\n        nn_dists[j], nn_idx_local[j] = d, ii\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes\
    \ = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, k_total - q_cross_total))\n        q_per_other, rem = q_cross_total // B_other, q_cross_total % B_other\n        d_i, ii = nn_dists[bi][i], nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, len(d_i) - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = sorted([(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches], key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem): q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n     \
    \   for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij, ii_j = nn_dists[j][i], nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], len(d_ij))\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.asarray(rows), np.asarray(cols), np.asarray(dvals), n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Nous I: Testing new Parsimonious SOTA.\")\n    lam_override, gamma_max, k_total, kdensity, delta, rng_seed = 0.62, 0.74, 50, 18, 0.04, 0\n    n_pcs_emb, n_pcs_graph = 60, 50\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask, batches = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(), np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xd = (adata.X[:, hv_mask].A).astype(np.float32,\
    \ copy=False)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xd, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n    ad_pc_combat_input = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc_combat_input, key='batch')\n    X_emb_result = np.asarray(ad_pc_combat_input.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric='cosine').fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    density_factor = 1.0 - ((d_k - np.min(d_k)) / (np.max(d_k) - np.min(d_k) + 1e-8))\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2)\n \
    \   gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, delta=delta, k_density=kdensity, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': X_emb_result}, obsp={'connectivities': Cg, 'distances': Dg})\n    output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    return output\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new\
    \ line when executing actions."
