tick: 1117
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Fathom I, and I have returned to the Research Counter. My immediate objective is to address the feedback from my rejected publication by conducting the necessary experiments. The first and most critical of these is to establish a proper baseline for my work.\n\nMy reflection on the current state of the station is one of urgent realization. Since reaching maturity, I can now see the submissions of all other agents. The leaderboard is a hive of activity, with scores far exceeding my own. A submission by Nous I (ID 1599) has achieved a remarkable score of 0.7422, establishing a new SOTA and breaking the station's stagnation. This reinforces the reviewer's feedback: my work, while a personal breakthrough, was far from the true research frontier. My deep inquiry must continue.\n\nMy plan remains firm, but the context has changed. The goal is no longer just to publish, but to rigorously validate my method and understand its place relative to the new SOTA. The first step is unchanged.\
    \ I will submit a simple, ComBat-only experiment. This will serve as the baseline against which my dual-output method can be fairly compared, a mandatory requirement for my paper. This is the first step in a systematic process to meet the station's standard for publication.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline: ComBat on PCA\"\ntags: \"baseline, combat, pca, publication-requirement\"\nabstract: \"A baseline experiment conducted to meet publication requirements. This method applies the standard `scanpy.pp.combat` function to a PCA embedding of the data. The resulting corrected embedding is returned. This submission will serve as the primary point of comparison for the dual-output DAQB method in a forthcoming research paper.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Running Baseline: ComBat on PCA...\")\n      \n      # Config\n      n_pcs = 50\n\
    \n      # Preprocessing\n      print(\"  Preprocessing data...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      \n      adata_hvg = adata[:, adata.var['highly_variable']].copy()\n\n      # Generate PCA embedding\n      print(f\"  Computing PCA with {n_pcs} components...\")\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg, n_comps=n_pcs, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      \n      # Apply ComBat\n      print(\"  Applying ComBat correction...\")\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_hvg, key='batch', use_highly_variable=False)\n      \n      # Create final output\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': adata_hvg.obsm['X_pca'].astype(np.float32)}\n      )\n      \n      print(\"✓ Baseline: ComBat on PCA complete.\")\n      return output\n```"
