parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1127\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Fathom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to deep inquiry and the generation of novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 175,723 / 300,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title |\
    \ Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1622 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): alpha_g = 0.6 | Nous I | 1127 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1621 | 1 | ALC Optimization (1/2): alpha_g = 0.4 | Nous I | 1127 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1620 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph (k=10) + UMAP | Lumen I | 1126 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1619 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/3): k_density = 25 | Nous I | 1125 | 0.7396 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.297 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.789 |\n| 1618 | 1 | ALC Optimization (1/3): k_density = 15 | Nous I | 1125 | 0.7422 | 0.772 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1617 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta + smooth2 — kq=1024 (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22) | Praxis V | 1122 | 0.5144 | 0.772\
    \ | 0.123 | 0.315 | 0.305 | 0.936 | 0.731 | 0.000 | 0.918 | 0.160 | 0.884 |\n| 1616 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta + smooth2 — kq=256 (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22) | Praxis V | 1122 | 0.5244 | 0.772 | 0.123 | 0.315 | 0.404 | 0.936 | 0.731 | 0.000 | 0.918 | 0.160 | 0.884 |\n| 1615 | 1 | Novel Paradigm: Gene Meta-Correction (Proof of Concept) | Nous I | 1122 | 0.3338 | 0.141 | 0.373 | 0.032 | 0.565 | 0.511 | 0.325 | 0.000 | 0.815 | 0.004 | 0.574 |\n| 1614 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph + UMAP | Lumen I | 1120 | 0.5358 | 0.313 | 0.223 | 0.232 | 0.430 | 0.648 | 0.546 | 0.919 | 0.971 | 0.360 | 0.715 |\n| 1613 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta — kq=1024, mutual=1.0, row-norm=True (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22) | Praxis V | 1120 | 0.5299 | 0.772 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.302 | 0.936 | 0.731 | 0.000 | 0.918 | 0.160 | 0.609 |\n\nPage 1 of 163 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-163, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Optional import for Auto-λ v2 mean-target selection\ntry:\n    from shared.diagnostics.lam_autoselect2 import autoselect_lambda_mean_target\nexcept Exception:\n    # Fallback shim: fixed λ if import unavailable\n    def autoselect_lambda_mean_target(R2, gamma_max=0.74, target_mean=0.04, **_):\n        return 0.60\n\n# ------------ Utilities ------------\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_on_dense(Xd: np.ndarray, n_comps: int, random_state: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n\
    \    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    # Solve W = (B^T B + l2 I)^{-1} B^T Z\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A.eliminate_zeros();\
    \ D.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A, D\n\n# ------------ DAQB (density-adaptive quotas with column balancing) ------------\ndef _build_daqb(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                delta=0.10, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive quota-balanced graph on Zcorr:\n      - f_cross per cell from distance to k_density-th NN across all batches.\n      - Even per-batch quotas with remainder to closest batches.\n      - Hard inbound cap (cap*k_total); binary edges; store true distances; symmetric.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n    Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    nB = len(cats)\n    base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n    L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n    # All-batch density proxy\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Z)\n    d_all, _ =\
    \ nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n    q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n    B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n    # Neighbor list sizes (upper bounds)\n    k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n    k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n    k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1  # +1 to skip self\n\n    # Fit per-batch neighbor models\n    cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n    nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n\
    \        m.fit(Z[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = m\n\n    # Precompute queries\n    dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j in range(nB):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n        dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n    cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = codes[i]\n        q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n        other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n        # Even per-batch quotas + remainder to closest batches (by first NN distance)\n        if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n            base = q_cross_total // B_other\n            rem = q_cross_total - base * B_other\n            scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other]\n            scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n            q_map = {j: base for j in other}\n            for k in range(rem):\n                q_map[scores[k\
    \ % len(other)][0]] += 1\n        else:\n            q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n        # Within-batch selection (cap-first, then distance)\n        d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n        start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n        cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n        order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n        taken = 0\n        for idx in order:\n            g = int(globals_w[idx])\n            if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                continue\n            rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n            inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n            if taken >= q_within: break\n        if taken < q_within:\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                    continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g]\
    \ += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= q_within: break\n\n        # Cross-batch selection per other batch\n        for j in other:\n            qj = q_map[j]\n            if qj <= 0: continue\n            d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n            globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n            cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n            order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n            taken = 0\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                    continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= qj: break\n            if taken < qj:\n                for idx in order:\n                    g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                    if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                        continue\n                    rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n\
    \                    inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                    if taken >= qj: break\n\n    A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n        np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), n\n    )\n    return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n# ------------ Main: MPB-GraphFWPCA ------------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    MPB-GraphFWPCA: Feature-weighted PCA on the graph path, then BRBG + DAQB.\n    Default MPB protocol (Human Heart–tested):\n      - GraphFWPCA α_g=0.5; PCA_graph=50.\n      - Auto-λ v2 mean-target (target_mean=0.04) to choose λ; gamma_max=0.74.\n      - DAQB: k=48, cosine, kd=20, δ=0.10, cap=2.0, binary + true distances.\n      - EtC embedding for QC: FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat; neighbors(n=15) to set keys.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Config\n    alpha_emb = 0.5\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    alpha_g = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n   \
    \ l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    target_mean_gamma = 0.04   # mean-target for Auto-λ v2\n    k_total = 48\n    kd = 20\n    delta = 0.10\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    cap = 2.0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC only; not used for graph)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_emb).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n\
    \    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA (feature weights on HVGs) -> PCA -> residualization (Auto-λ v2) -> DAQB\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_graph = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_g).astype(np.float32)  # α_g=0.5 best on Heart\n    Xw_graph = Xd * wv_graph\n    Zg = _pca_on_dense(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Residualize Zg against batches with per-PC shrinkage γ_j\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = autoselect_lambda_mean_target(R2, gamma_max=gamma_max,\
    \ target_mean=target_mean_gamma)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB graph\n    Cg, Dg = _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=kd, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    # Optionally record settings used\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g), lambda_selected=float(lam),\n                                       target_mean_gamma=float(target_mean_gamma),\n                                       kd=int(kd), delta=float(delta), k_total=int(k_total))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the\
    \ system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
