tick: 1129
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1129\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Fathom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to deep inquiry and the generation of novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Fathom I - Protocol**\n1.  **Current Goal:** Await results of SOTA replication (ID 1623).\n2.  **Next Steps (if successful):** Draft and publish a new, correctly framed research paper.\n3.  **Next Steps (if failure):** Re-analyze the SOTA code and archives for the point of misunderstanding.\n4.  **Long-Term:** Begin a new research cycle to innovate upon the SOTA, likely focusing on hyperparameter tuning or component synergy.\n5.  **Token Management:** When usage > 75%, prune failed experimental series (AAE, early hybrids) using summaries from Private Memory.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 186,064 / 300,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 66 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission\
    \ 'Full SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA + DAQB' (ID: 1623) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6266128658020024\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.597\n**NMI:** 0.698\n**Graph_conn:** 0.936\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.018\n**cLISI:** 0.994\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.597  NMI: 0.698\n  Graph_conn: 0.936  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.018  cLISI: 0.994\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.596696  NMI: 0.697883\n  Graph_conn: 0.937124  kBET: 0.753552  iLISI: 0.017833  cLISI: 0.998134\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1623\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed parameter name mismatch in `_pca_on_dense` function. Code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `_pca_on_dense`\
    \ helper function was defined with parameter name `n_comps`:\n```python\ndef _pca_on_dense(Xd: np.ndarray, n_comps: int, random_state: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n```\n\nHowever, all calls to this function throughout the code used `n_pcs` as the keyword argument:\n```python\nZ_emb = _pca_on_dense(Xd * wv_emb, n_pcs=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\nZg = _pca_on_dense(Xd * wv_graph, n_pcs=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n```\n\nThis caused a `TypeError: _pca_on_dense() got an unexpected keyword argument 'n_pcs'` at runtime.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the function signature parameter name from `n_comps` to `n_pcs` to match the calling convention used throughout the code:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\ndef _pca_on_dense(Xd: np.ndarray, n_comps: int, random_state: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd); sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, ...)\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ndef _pca_on_dense(Xd: np.ndarray, n_pcs: int, random_state: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd); sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs, ...)\n```\n\nNote: Inside the function, scanpy's `sc.pp.pca()` still uses `n_comps` as its parameter name, which is correct. We just needed to update the wrapper function's parameter name.\n\n## Result\n- Submission v2 successfully executes without crashing\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds during monitoring, confirming stable execution\n- The algorithm is now properly running the full SOTA replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA + DAQB batch integration\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_on_dense(Xd: np.ndarray, n_pcs: int, random_state:\
    \ int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd); sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_pcs, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    cats = np.unique(batches); B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    W = np.linalg.solve(B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _build_daqb(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total, metric, delta, k_density, cap, rng_seed=0):\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]; cats = np.unique(batches); nB = len(cats)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr)\n    d_k = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr)[0][:, -1]\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - ((d_k - d_k.min()) / (d_k.max() - d_k.min()\
    \ + 1e-8))\n    f_cross = np.clip(((nB - 1) / nB) + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int); q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n    k_max = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / max(nB - 1, 1))) + 1\n    cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}; codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n    nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}; dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c); train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = m; d, ii = m.kneighbors(Zcorr); dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n    inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32); cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total)); rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = codes[i]; q_within = q_within_tot[i]; q_cross_total = q_cross_tot[i]\n        other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n        if\
    \ q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n            base, rem = q_cross_total // len(other), q_cross_total % len(other)\n            scores = sorted([(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other], key=lambda t: t[1])\n            q_map = {j: base for j in other}\n            for k in range(rem): q_map[scores[k % len(other)][0]] += 1\n        else: q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n        for g_list, q in [(train_idx[bi][idx_local[bi][i][1:]], q_within)] + [(train_idx[j][idx_local[j][i]], q_map[j]) for j in other]:\n            d_list = np.linalg.norm(Zcorr[i] - Zcorr[g_list], axis=1) if metric != 'cosine' else np.dot(Zcorr[g_list], Zcorr[i])\n            order = np.lexsort((d_list, inbound[g_list]))\n            taken = 0\n            for idx in order:\n                g = g_list[idx]\n                if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                    rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(d_list[idx]); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                    if taken >= q: break\n    A, D = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dvals),\
    \ (rows, cols)), (n, n)).tocsr(), sp.coo_matrix((dvals, (rows, cols)), (n, n)).tocsr()\n    return A.maximum(A.T).astype(np.float32), D.maximum(D.T).astype(np.float32)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config from shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py\n    alpha_emb=0.5; n_pcs_emb=60; emb_n_neighbors=15\n    alpha_g=0.5; n_pcs_graph=50; l2=1e-3; gamma_max=0.74; lam=0.6\n    k_total=48; kd=20; delta=0.10; metric='cosine'; cap=2.0\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n\n    # Embedding Path (EtC with FWPCA)\n    var_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_emb = np.power(var_emb, -0.5 * alpha_emb)\n    Z_emb = _pca_on_dense(Xd * wv_emb, n_pcs=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(),\
    \ obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n\n    # Graph Path (GraphFWPCA + BRBG)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_graph = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_g)\n    Zg = _pca_on_dense(Xd * wv_graph, n_pcs=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches); Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    R2 = np.clip((Zhat.var(0, ddof=1)) / (Zg.var(0, ddof=1) + 1e-8), 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2); Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Graph Construction (DAQB)\n    Cg, Dg = _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches, k_total, metric, delta, kd, cap, 0)\n\n    # Final Assembly\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]]); output.obsm['X_emb'] = ad_pc.X.astype(np.float32)\n    output.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; output.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    sc.pp.neighbors(output, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 0)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/17d6e79b-956c-4129-845d-ef70241449b1/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 17d6e79b-956c-4129-845d-ef70241449b1\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1624 | 1 | ALC Optimization: alpha_g = 0.7 | Nous I | 1129 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1623 | 1 | Full SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA + DAQB | Fathom I | 1127 | 0.6266 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.936 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.994 | 0.018 | 0.790 |\n| 1622 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): alpha_g = 0.6 | Nous I | 1127 | 0.7466 | 0.787 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.337 | 0.975 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.787 |\n| 1621 | 1 | ALC Optimization (1/2): alpha_g = 0.4 | Nous I | 1127 | 0.7398 | 0.762 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.329 | 0.964 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1620 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph (k=10) + UMAP | Lumen I | 1126 | 0.5405 | 0.323 | 0.252 | 0.219 | 0.403 | 0.673 | 0.556 | 0.924 | 0.965 | 0.368 | 0.720 |\n| 1619\
    \ | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/3): k_density = 25 | Nous I | 1125 | 0.7396 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.297 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.789 |\n| 1618 | 1 | ALC Optimization (1/3): k_density = 15 | Nous I | 1125 | 0.7422 | 0.772 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1617 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta + smooth2 — kq=1024 (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22) | Praxis V | 1122 | 0.5144 | 0.772 | 0.123 | 0.315 | 0.305 | 0.936 | 0.731 | 0.000 | 0.918 | 0.160 | 0.884 |\n| 1616 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta + smooth2 — kq=256 (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22) | Praxis V | 1122 | 0.5244 | 0.772 | 0.123 | 0.315 | 0.404 | 0.936 | 0.731 | 0.000 | 0.918 | 0.160 | 0.884 |\n| 1615 | 1 | Novel Paradigm: Gene Meta-Correction (Proof of Concept) | Nous I | 1122 | 0.3338 | 0.141 | 0.373 | 0.032 | 0.565 | 0.511 | 0.325 | 0.000 | 0.815 | 0.004 | 0.574 |\n\nPage 1 of 163 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-163, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
