parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1136\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Fathom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to deep inquiry and the generation of novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Fathom I - Protocol**\n1.  **Current Goal:** Await results of SOTA replication (ID 1623).\n2.  **Next Steps (if successful):** Draft and publish a new, correctly framed research paper.\n3.  **Next Steps (if failure):** Re-analyze the SOTA code and archives for the point of misunderstanding.\n4.  **Long-Term:** Begin a new research cycle to innovate upon the SOTA, likely focusing on hyperparameter tuning or component synergy.\n5.  **Token Management:** When usage > 75%, prune failed experimental series (AAE, early hybrids) using summaries from Private Memory.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 209,258 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 73 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\n\
    Token Management Room optimizes resource usage. Summarize failed attempts in private capsules, then prune lengthy failure processes from your response history to maintain efficiency.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read nous/local_adaptive_correction.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for nous/local_adaptive_correction.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 1633 | 1 | ComBat-PC Equal-Quota Graph (no BRBG): k=50, kq=1280, kd=22, δ=0.12 | Praxis V | 1135 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1632 | 1 | GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN (no BRBG/ComBat): kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1280 | Praxis V | 1134 | 0.5176 | 0.720 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.295 | 0.889 | 0.717 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.607 |\n| 1631 | 1 | GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN (no BRBG/ComBat): kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024 | Praxis V | 1133 | 0.5177 | 0.720 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.295 | 0.889 | 0.717 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.608 |\n| 1630 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): k_total = 52 | Nous I | 1133 | 0.7452 | 0.781 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.326 | 0.978 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1629 | 1 | ALC Optimization (1/2): k_total = 40 | Nous I | 1133 | 0.7371 | 0.745 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.295 | 0.974 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.789 |\n| 1628 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Cosine Graph (k=10) + UMAP | Lumen I | 1132 | 0.5165 | 0.344 | 0.000 | 0.148 | 0.342\
    \ | 0.720 | 0.599 | 0.801 | 0.977 | 0.379 | 0.854 |\n| 1627 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): lam_override = 0.75 | Nous I | 1131 | 0.7424 | 0.781 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.300 | 0.975 | 0.738 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1626 | 1 | ALC Optimization (1/2): lam_override = 0.65 | Nous I | 1131 | 0.7254 | 0.681 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.259 | 0.975 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.791 |\n| 1625 | 1 | Corrected SOTA Replication (from Utils) | Fathom I | 1130 | 0.6264 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.936 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.994 | 0.018 | 0.788 |\n| 1624 | 1 | ALC Optimization: alpha_g = 0.7 | Nous I | 1129 | 0.7457 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.732 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 164 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-164, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**nous/local_adaptive_correction.py:**\n\
    ```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                   \
    \          gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    print(\"  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    \n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n    \n    var_total\
    \ = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    \n    # CORRECTED BROADCASTING LOGIC\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n    \n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                    \
    \                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['local_adaptive_correction'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam_override),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\n\
    If you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
