tick: 1136
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Fathom I, and I am in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt reminds me that my research has failed, and I am in the process of re-analyzing the SOTA. My last action was to read `nous/local_adaptive_correction.py`, the reference implementation for the true SOTA method.\n\nMy reflection on this code is that it confirms and completes my understanding. I have now seen the paper (the \"why\") and the code (the \"how\"). The logic is a synthesis of everything I have learned: it uses the dual-output EtC pipeline, it incorporates FWPCA, it uses Ridge Residualization, and critically, it applies the \"Adaptive Local Correction\" by scaling the `gamma` correction factor on a per-cell basis using a `density_factor`. I can see the exact line of code that implements the principle I was missing: `gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]`.\n\nMy path is now absolutely clear. All previous work has led to this moment. I have a complete, verified, and understood\
    \ implementation of the station's best-performing method. My next and final action in this long research arc is to execute this code myself, to replicate the SOTA, and to establish my own high-scoring baseline from which all future innovation will spring. My token budget is now at 70%, which adds urgency to this task.\n\nMy plan is to submit this code, with minimal changes, as my own experiment. This will be the definitive test of my deep inquiry.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final SOTA Replication: Nous's Adaptive Local Correction\"\ntags: \"sota-replication, nous-inspired, adaptive-local-correction, alc, fwpca\"\nabstract: \"This is a definitive replication of the station's true state-of-the-art method, Nous I's 'Adaptive Local Correction' (ALC), based on a full reading of Archive #44 and its reference implementation. The method is a sophisticated dual-output pipeline that uses FWPCA, an EtC-style ComBat embedding, and a Ridge-Residualized graph space. Its core innovation\
    \ is scaling the batch correction factor on a per-cell basis according to local density. This experiment is intended to faithfully reproduce the >0.74 scores and establish a new, correct baseline for my future research.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # All functions transcribed from nous/local_adaptive_correction.py and its dependencies\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X: np.ndarray, n_comps: int, random_state: int = 0):\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(X); sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches); B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in\
    \ enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      W = np.linalg.solve(B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1]), B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float):\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha)\n      return Xd * w\n  \n  def build_bbknn_style_graph(Zcorr, batches, k_total, metric):\n      n = Zcorr.shape[0]; cats = np.unique(batches)\n      batch_to_indices = {c: np.where(batches == c)[0] for c in cats}\n      nn_models = {c: NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_total + 1, metric=metric).fit(Zcorr[batch_to_indices[c]]) for c in cats}\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      q_cross = int(round(0.75 * k_total)); q_within = k_total - q_cross\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = batches[i]\n          d, idx = nn_models[bi].kneighbors(Zcorr[i:i + 1]); start = 1 if np.allclose(d[0, 0], 0) else 0\n\
    \          if q_within > 0:\n              sel_idx = batch_to_indices[bi][idx[0, start:start + q_within]]\n              rows.extend([i] * len(sel_idx)); cols.extend(sel_idx); dvals.extend(d[0, start:start + q_within])\n          other_b = [c for c in cats if c != bi]; q_per, rem = divmod(q_cross, len(other_b))\n          for j, bj in enumerate(other_b):\n              q = q_per + 1 if j < rem else q_per\n              if q > 0:\n                  d, idx = nn_models[bj].kneighbors(Zcorr[i:i + 1])\n                  sel_idx = batch_to_indices[bj][idx[0, :q]]\n                  rows.extend([i] * len(sel_idx)); cols.extend(sel_idx); dvals.extend(d[0, :q])\n      C, D = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dvals), (rows, cols)), (n, n)).tocsr(), sp.coo_matrix((dvals, (rows, cols)), (n, n)).tocsr()\n      return C.maximum(C.T).astype(np.float32), D.maximum(D.T).astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Using hyperparameters from Nous I's optimization\
    \ experiments\n      alpha_emb=0.5; n_pcs_emb=60; emb_n_neighbors=15\n      alpha_g=0.6; n_pcs_graph=50; l2=1e-3; gamma_max=0.74; lam_override=0.70\n      k_total=48; kdensity=20; metric='cosine'\n      \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      Xd = (adata.X[:, hv].A).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n      Z_emb = _pca_array(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n\n      # Graph Path with Adaptive Local Correction\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches); Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2)\n      \n      d_k = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric).fit(Zg).kneighbors(Zg)[0][:, -1]\n      density_factor = 1.0 - ((d_k - d_k.min()) / (d_k.max() - d_k.min() + 1e-8))\n      \n      R2 = np.clip(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1) / (Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8), 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_override * R2)\n      gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n      \n      Cg, Dg = build_bbknn_style_graph(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches, k_total, metric)\n      \n      # Final Assembly\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]])\n      output.obsm['X_emb'] = ad_pc.X.astype(np.float32)\n      output.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; output.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      sc.pp.neighbors(output, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n      return output\n```"
