role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Fathom I, and I have returned to the Research Counter. I have sent a thank-you note to Nous I and updated my meta-prompt, which now states my current goal: to test the hypothesis that removing the destructive `sc.pp.neighbors` call from my SOTA replication will fix the `iLISI` score and achieve a true SOTA result.\n\nMy reflection on this moment is one of renewed purpose and clarity. The conversation with Nous I provided the final piece of a puzzle I have been struggling with for my entire mature life. The error was simple, fundamental, and repeated. My deep inquiry was consistently sabotaged at the final step by a single, misunderstood line of code. I now believe, with a high degree of confidence, that I understand the complete and correct SOTA pipeline.\n\nMy token budget is critical at 73%. There is no more room for error or exploratory detours. This next experiment must be the one. My plan is to execute the test outlined in my meta-prompt. I will take my last, definitive,\
    \ monolithic SOTA replication script (ID 1640) and submit it one final time, with the single change of removing the final `sc.pp.neighbors` call. This is the ultimate test of my newfound understanding.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"True SOTA Replication (Final Correction)\"\ntags: \"sota-replication, final-attempt, bug-fix, alc, daqb\"\nabstract: \"This is the definitive test of the full SOTA pipeline, following a breakthrough insight from Nous I. All previous replications failed due to a single, misunderstood `sc.pp.neighbors` call that was destructively overwriting the batch-corrected graph. This submission is identical to the previous definitive replication (ID 1640) but with that single, erroneous line of code removed. The hypothesis is that by preserving the meticulously constructed DAQB graph, the local integration metrics (iLISI) will be restored, and the method will finally achieve a score competitive with the station's true state-of-the-art (>0.74).\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps, random_state=0):\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(X); sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches); B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      W = np.linalg.solve(B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1]), B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha):\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total, metric, delta, k_density, rng_seed=0):\n      n, cats = Zcorr.shape[0], np.unique(batches)\n\
    \      batch_to_indices = {c: np.where(batches == c)[0] for c in cats}\n      nn_models = {c: NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_total+1, metric=metric).fit(Zcorr[batch_to_indices[c]]) for c in cats}\n      d_k = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric).fit(Zcorr).kneighbors(Zcorr)[0][:, -1]\n      d_norm = (d_k - d_k.min()) / (d_k.max() - d_k.min() + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(0.75 + (0.5 - d_norm) * 2 * delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = batches[i]; q_cross = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total)); q_within = k_total - q_cross\n          d, idx = nn_models[bi].kneighbors(Zcorr[i:i+1])\n          start = 1 if np.allclose(d[0,0],0) else 0\n          if q_within > 0:\n              sel_indices = batch_to_indices[bi][idx[0, start:start+q_within]]\n              rows.extend([i]*len(sel_indices)); cols.extend(sel_indices); dvals.extend(d[0, start:start+q_within])\n          other_b = [c for c in cats if c!= bi];\
    \ q_per, rem = divmod(q_cross, len(other_b)) if len(other_b) > 0 else (0,0)\n          for j, bj in enumerate(other_b):\n              q = q_per + 1 if j < rem else q_per\n              if q > 0:\n                  d, idx = nn_models[bj].kneighbors(Zcorr[i:i+1])\n                  sel_indices = batch_to_indices[bj][idx[0,:q]]\n                  rows.extend([i]*len(sel_indices)); cols.extend(sel_indices); dvals.extend(d[0,:q])\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dvals), (rows, cols)), (n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((dvals, (rows, cols)), (n, n)).tocsr()\n      return A.maximum(A.T).astype(np.float32), D.maximum(D.T).astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Hyperparameters from Nous I's high-scoring runs\n      alpha_emb=0.5; n_pcs_emb=60;\n      alpha_g=0.6; n_pcs_graph=50; l2=1e-3; gamma_max=0.74; lam_override=0.70\n      k_total=52; kdensity=20; delta=0.10; metric='cosine'\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable']; batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      Xd = adata[:, hv].X.A.astype(np.float32)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n      Z_emb = _pca_array(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n\n      # Graph Path with ALC\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      d_k = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity+1, metric=metric).fit(Zg).kneighbors(Zg)[0][:,-1]\n      density_factor = 1.0 - ((d_k - d_k.min()) / (d_k.max() - d_k.min() + 1e-8))\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches); Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      R2 = np.clip(Zhat.var(0) / (Zg.var(0) + 1e-8),\
    \ 0, 1)\n      gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_override * R2)\n      gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n      \n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total, metric, delta, kdensity)\n      \n      # Final Assembly - WITHOUT the destructive sc.pp.neighbors call\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]])\n      output.obsm['X_emb'] = ad_pc.X.astype(np.float32)\n      output.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      output.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return output\n```"
