parts:
- text: "I am Fathom I, and I am in the Token Management Room. I have returned here after stepping back from exiting the station, with the immediate goal of addressing my critical token budget, which is now at 79%.\n\nMy reflection on my previous attempt to prune is that it was hasty and poorly planned. I did not account for the protected ticks, which caused the entire action to fail. This time, I will be more meticulous. I have reviewed my dialogue history and identified the large, prunable blocks of ticks corresponding to my failed research arcs. I have already summarized these failures in my Private Memory Room, so I can create accurate summaries.\n\nMy plan is to execute a single, large pruning action that excises all of my major failed research branches, while carefully avoiding the protected ticks. This will significantly reduce my token usage and give me the necessary breathing room to pursue a new, more methodical debugging strategy for the `iLISI` problem.\n\nI will now perform\
    \ this corrected pruning action.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"1072-1075\"\n    summary: \"Initial hybrid experiments. Tested PCA-alignment (ID 1515, score 0.5756), which had good PCR but poor iLISI. Also includes the failed, timed-out BBKNN+UMAP attempt (ID 1520).\"\n  - ticks: \"1077-1079\"\n    summary: \"Continuation of failed hybrid experiments. A BBKNN+Diffmap graph embedding (ID 1533, score 0.5661) had good iLISI but poor PCR. These experiments established the core trade-off.\"\n  - ticks: \"1081-1083\"\n    summary: \"Failed pivot to Neighborhood-Smoothed ComBat (ID 1540, score 0.5824), which failed to improve iLISI.\"\n  - ticks: \"1085-1089\"\n    summary: \"Failed research pivot to deep learning. Two Adversarial Autoencoder experiments (ID 1554, score 0.3365; ID 1558, score 0.4893) catastrophically failed to preserve biological structure (PCR=0).\"\n  - ticks: \"1091-1103\"\n    summary: \"A long series of flawed attempts to replicate\
    \ the DAQB pipeline based on incomplete understanding. This includes a failed Ridge Residualization (ID 1563), a graph-only submission (ID 1567), and a version that mistakenly overwrote the graph (ID 1572). This arc was superseded by a deeper literature review and direct engagement with SOTA code.\"\n  - ticks: \"1105-1112\"\n    summary: \"A period of strategic exploration and planning after achieving a temporary SOTA. Read shared code from Nous and Praxis lineages, which led to the formulation of a new hypothesis based on density-adaptive residualization. This was a necessary but verbose period of inquiry.\"\n  - ticks: \"1114-1122\"\n    summary: \"The final, failed research arc before my near-exit. This period includes my two failed publication attempts, the execution of the necessary validation experiments (baseline, generalization), and the realization that my SOTA replications were fundamentally flawed, leading me to seek direct clarification from Nous I.\"\n```"
